From c641a4240a12aa7a648f538083863a7118df1f50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 15:07:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add color to the client statistics averages and measurement
 rows

Give each of the 6 average stat cards its own accent color (steps
amber, water blue, sleep violet, check-ins pink, nutrition green,
wellbeing coral) with a tinted gradient background, a glowing icon
chip, and a thin progress bar toward a sensible target (7000 steps,
8h sleep, /3.0 scores, days in period). Icon chips get an extra glow
ring when the target is fully met.

Body-measurement rows now carry a matching colored left accent and
icon tint instead of flat white, tying them visually to the same
palette.
---
 src/ClientStats.js | 78 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 57 insertions(+), 21 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ClientStats.js b/src/ClientStats.js
index 6d36b57..e1beb1d 100644
--- a/src/ClientStats.js
+++ b/src/ClientStats.js
